   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>\r\n<div>I&#39;m using tidyLPA 1.0.0 with mclust. I use it to get some values I can&#39;t get directly from mclust, like AIC or Tolerance).</div><div>I&#39;m having a problem and I wonder if you could help me.</div><div><br></div><div>My model is VVE and my df is called lpa.</div><div>If I run</div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt;outline:currentcolor none medium;border:medium none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:15px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre-wrap\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">lpa %&gt;%\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre-wrap\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">           estimate_profiles(n_profiles=models.to.test)\r\n</span><span style=\"outline:currentcolor none medium;border:medium none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap\">tidyLPA analysis using mclust: \r\n\r\n<font size=\"1\"> Model Classes AIC       BIC       Entropy prob_min prob_max n_min n_max BLRT_p\r\n 1     2       25441.423 25547.015 0.807   0.022    0.160    0.312 0.688 0.010 \r\n 1     3       24681.423 24825.918 0.800   0.075    0.890    0.089 0.489 0.010 \r\n 1     4       24424.577 24607.973 0.777   0.000    0.029    0.027 0.406 0.010 \r\n 1     5       24274.329 24496.628 0.787   0.000    0.016    0.028 0.407 0.010 \r\n 1     6       24248.393 24509.595 0.682   0.000    0.065    0.027 0.314 0.010 \r\n 1     7       24212.576 24512.680 0.650   0.082    0.140    0.026 0.312 0.010 </font>\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Warning message:\r\n\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">One or more analyses resulted in warnings! Examine these analyses carefully: model_1_class_4, model_1_class_5, model_1_class_6 </span></span></pre></div><div><br></div><div>it works fine. <br></div><div><br></div><div>But if I add the argument models=6 or <br><pre style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px\">variances = &quot;varying&quot;, covariances = &quot;varying&quot;\r\n\r\n</pre></div><div>I get an error:</div><div><br></div><div><pre style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt;outline:currentcolor none medium;border:medium none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:15px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\"><span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre-wrap\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">lpa %&gt;%\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre-wrap\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">           estimate_profiles(n_profiles=models.to.test, models=6)\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">The &#39;variances&#39;/&#39;covariances&#39; arguments were ignored in favor of the &#39;models&#39; argument.\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Error in MclustBootstrap(out$model, nboot = 100, type = &quot;bs&quot;, verbose = FALSE) : \r\n  object must be of class &#39;Mclust&#39; or &#39;densityMclust&#39;</span></span></span></span></pre></div><div><br></div><div>I get the same error if I run the code from the example in the documentation for <span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);display:inline;float:none\">estimate_profiles {tidyLPA}</span></div><div><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:sans-serif;font-size:13px;font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;line-height:normal;text-align:start;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;white-space:normal;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255);display:inline;float:none\"><br></span></div><pre style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;font-size:10pt;outline:currentcolor none medium;border:medium none;word-break:break-all;margin:0px;white-space:pre-wrap;line-height:15px;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-style:normal;font-variant:normal;font-weight:normal;letter-spacing:normal;text-indent:0px;text-transform:none;word-spacing:0px;background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"><span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre-wrap\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\"># Example 3:\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre-wrap\">&gt; </span><span style=\"color:blue\">iris_sample %&gt;%\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre-wrap\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">    subset(select = c(&quot;Sepal.Length&quot;, &quot;Sepal.Width&quot;,\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre-wrap\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">                      &quot;Petal.Length&quot;)) %&gt;%\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre-wrap\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">    estimate_profiles(n_profiles = 1:4, variances = c(&quot;equal&quot;, &quot;varying&quot;),\r\n</span><span style=\"color:blue;white-space:pre-wrap\">+ </span><span style=\"color:blue\">                      covariances = c(&quot;zero&quot;, &quot;zero&quot;))\r\n</span><span style=\"color:rgb(197,6,11)\">Error in MclustBootstrap(out$model, nboot = 100, type = &quot;bs&quot;, verbose = FALSE) : \r\n  object must be of class &#39;Mclust&#39; or &#39;densityMclust&#39;</span></span></pre><div> </div><div>Do you have an idea of which the problem is? Or if I can get AIC and Tolerance directly from mclust?</div>\r\n\r\n</div><div><br></div><div><div dir=\"ltr\" class=\"gmail_signature\" data-smartmail=\"gmail_signature\">Ricardo Gouveia Rodrigues<br>Universidade da Beira Interior<br>Covilhã<br>Portugal</div></div></div>\r\n"
    ]
   ]
